{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "Stellar Tags API",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "OpenAPI specification for the Stellar Tags API. Covers the documented endpoints for tags, addresses, activity, and stats. API errors use a stable envelope with a machine-readable code and retryable flag; validation details contain only field names and safe messages.\n\n## Error catalog and recovery guidance\n\nEvery error response uses the `Error` envelope. Clients should map `error.code` to a central code-to-message catalog that provides an actionable, accessible message, remediation steps, and retry behavior. The catalog must:\n\n- Preserve a safe fallback for unknown codes (generic message, no server internals).\n- Never surface stack traces, SQL, upstream payloads, or internal identifiers.\n- Use `error.retryable` to decide whether to offer a retry action; when `retryable` is `true` clients may retry with backoff, otherwise they must not auto-retry.\n- Display `reference_id` (when present) to the user so support can correlate the failure. `reference_id` is a safe, opaque, non-sensitive identifier; it is never a secret and never contains internal details.\n- `correlation_id` may be echoed for tracing and is also safe to display.\n\n## Idempotency contract\n\nState-changing requests (tag create/update/delete/restore, payment submission) accept an optional `X-Idempotency-Key` request header. When supplied:\n\n- The server deduplicates requests sharing the same key for the same authenticated principal and operation.\n- A replayed request returns the original outcome and sets `X-Idempotent-Replay: true`; a first-time request sets `X-Idempotent-Replay: false` (or omits it).\n- Keys are scoped and expire; clients must generate a fresh key per logical operation and reuse it only for retries of that same operation.\n- Cross-tab coordination shares only non-sensitive operation references (never credentials or payment details) and relies on backend idempotency to prevent duplicate payment attempts; stale coordination state expires and clients resume or warn instead of re-submitting.\n\n## Soft-delete, restore, and username reuse semantics\n\n- **Reservation window**: when a tag (username) is soft-deleted, its name is reserved for a fixed `SOFT_DELETE_RESERVATION_DAYS` (default 30 days) from `deletedAt`. During this window the name cannot be claimed by any other owner.\n- **Restoration proof**: restoring a soft-deleted tag requires the original owner's authenticated identity (bearer token whose subject matches the tag's `ownerId`). The restore request must reference the tag id and the `deletedAt` value observed at deletion time; a mismatch (stale or already-restored) is rejected with `409 Conflict`.\n- **Post-expiry reuse**: once the reservation window elapses, the name becomes reusable. A new registration may claim it; the prior soft-deleted record is retained for audit but can no longer be restored (`410 Gone`).\n- **Transactional transitions**: delete, restore, and registration are enforced transactionally (row-level lock on the name). Concurrent delete/restore/registration cannot produce multiple active owners; losers receive `409 Conflict`.",
    "license": {
      "name": "MIT"
    }
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "http://localhost:3000",
      "description": "Local development server"
    },
    {
      "url": "https://api.stellartags.example",
      "description": "Production server"
    }
  ],
  "tags": [
    { "name": "Tags", "description": "Stellar address tag operations" },
    { "name": "Addresses", "description": "Stellar address lookups" },
    { "name": "Activity", "description": "Activity feed with cursor pagination" },
    { "name": "Stats", "description": "Aggregate platform statistics" },
    { "name": "Admin", "description": "Administrative endpoints" }
  ],
  "paths": {
    "/health": {
      "get": {
        "tags": ["Platform"],
        "summary": "Check platform health",
        "operationId": "getHealth",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "All configured dependencies are healthy",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HealthStatus" }
              }
            }
          },
          "503": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/ApiErrorResponse" }
        }
      }
    },
    "/federation": {
      "get": {
        "tags": ["Addresses"],
        "summary": "Resolve a federation name or address",
        "operationId": "getFederation",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "q",
            "in": "query",
            "required": true,
            "schema": { "type": "string" }
          },
          {
            "name": "type",
            "in": "query",
            "schema": { "type": "string", "enum": ["id", "name"] }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Resolved federation identity",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/FederationEntry" }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/ApiErrorResponse" },
          "404": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/ApiErrorResponse" },
          "500": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/ApiErrorResponse" },
          "502": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/ApiErrorResponse" },
          "503": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/ApiErrorResponse" }
        }
      }
    },
    "/lookup": {
      "get": {
        "tags": ["Addresses"],
        "summary": "Look up registered usernames",
        "operationId": "lookupUsernames",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "address",
            "in": "query",
            "schema": { "type": "string" }
          },
          {
            "name": "search",
            "in": "query",
            "schema": { "type": "string" }
          },
          {
            "name": "all",
            "in": "query",
            "schema": { "type": "boolean" }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Lookup result",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/LookupResult" }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/ApiErrorResponse" },
          "404": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/ApiErrorResponse" },
          "500": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/ApiErrorResponse" },
          "503": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/ApiErrorResponse" }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/tags": {
      "get": {
        "tags": ["Tags"],
        "summary": "List tags",
        "operationId": "listTags",
        "parameters": [
          { "$ref": "#/components/parameters/PageParam" },
          { "$ref": "#/components/parameters/LimitParam" },
          { "name": "q", "in": "query", "description": "Search query", "schema": { "type": "string" } }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "A paginated list of tags",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/TagList" }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/BadRequest" }
        }
      },
      "post": {
        "tags": ["Tags"],
        "summary": "Create a tag",
        "operationId": "createTag",
        "description": "Registers a new tag (username). If the name was soft-deleted and its reservation window has not expired, registration is rejected with `409 Conflict`. Once the window expires the name is reusable. Supports idempotent submission via `X-Idempotency-Key`; replays return the original outcome with `X-Idempotent-Replay: true`.",
        "parameters": [
          { "$ref": "#/components/parameters/IdempotencyKeyParam" }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/TagInput" }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "201": {
            "description": "Tag created",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Tag" }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/BadRequest" },
          "401": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" },
          "409": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/Conflict" }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/tags/{id}": {
      "parameters": [
        { "$ref": "#/components/parameters/TagIdParam" }
      ],
      "get": {
        "tags": ["Tags"],
        "summary": "Get a tag by id",
        "operationId": "getTag",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Tag details",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Tag" }
              }
            }
          },
          "404": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/NotFound" }
        }
      },
      "patch": {
        "tags": ["Tags"],
        "summary": "Update a tag",
        "operationId": "updateTag",
        "description": "Supports idempotent submission via `X-Idempotency-Key`; replays return the original outcome with `X-Idempotent-Replay: true`.",
        "parameters": [
          { "$ref": "#/components/parameters/IdempotencyKeyParam" }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/TagInput" }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Updated tag",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Tag" }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/BadRequest" },
          "401": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" },
          "404": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/NotFound" }
        }
      },
      "delete": {
        "tags": ["Tags"],
        "summary": "Soft-delete a tag",
        "operationId": "deleteTag",
        "description": "Soft-deletes the tag and starts the reservation window (`SOFT_DELETE_RESERVATION_DAYS`, default 30 days) during which the name cannot be reused. The transition is transactional; concurrent deletes/restores/registrations cannot create multiple owners. Supports idempotent submission via `X-Idempotency-Key`; replays return the original outcome with `X-Idempotent-Replay: true`.",
        "parameters": [
          { "$ref": "#/components/parameters/IdempotencyKeyParam" }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "204": { "description": "Tag soft-deleted" },
          "401": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" },
          "404": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/NotFound" },
          "409": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/Conflict" }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/tags/{id}/restore": {
      "parameters": [
        { "$ref": "#/components/parameters/TagIdParam" }
      ],
      "post": {
        "tags": ["Tags"],
        "summary": "Restore a soft-deleted tag",
        "operationId": "restoreTag",
        "description": "Restores a soft-deleted tag within its reservation window. Requires the original owner's authenticated identity and the `deletedAt` value observed at deletion time as restoration proof. Fails with `409 Conflict` on stale/already-restored state and `410 Gone` after the reservation window expires. Supports idempotent submission via `X-Idempotency-Key`; replays return the original outcome with `X-Idempotent-Replay: true`.",
        "security": [{ "bearerAuth": [] }],
        "parameters": [
          { "$ref": "#/components/parameters/IdempotencyKeyParam" }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/RestoreTagInput" }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Tag restored",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Tag" }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/BadRequest" },
          "401": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" },
          "403": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/Forbidden" },
          "404": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/NotFound" },
          "409": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/Conflict" },
          "410": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/Gone" }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/addresses/{address}": {
      "get": {
        "tags": ["Addresses"],
        "summary": "Get tags for a Stellar address",
        "operationId": "getAddressTags",
        "parameters": [
          { "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AddressParam" }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Tags associated with the address",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/TagList" }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/BadRequest" },
          "404": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/NotFound" }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/activity": {
      "get": {
        "tags": ["Activity"],
        "summary": "List activity feed entries",
        "operationId": "listActivity",
        "parameters": [
          { "$ref": "#/components/parameters/CursorParam" },
          { "$ref": "#/components/parameters/LimitParam" }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Cursor-paginated activity feed",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ActivityList" }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/BadRequest" }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/stats": {
      "get": {
        "tags": ["Stats"],
        "summary": "Get platform statistics",
        "description": "Returns aggregate statistics served from the refreshable reporting read model. The response includes the source watermark and refresh status so clients can reason about staleness. Reporting refreshes run asynchronously and never block payment writes.",
        "operationId": "getStats",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Aggregate platform statistics from the reporting read model",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Stats" }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/admin/stats": {
      "get": {
        "tags": ["Admin"],
        "summary": "Get admin statistics",
        "operationId": "getAdminStats",
        "security": [{ "bearerAuth": [] }],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Administrative statistics",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Stats" }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" },
          "403": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/Forbidden" }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/admin/stats/refresh": {
      "post": {
        "tags": ["Admin"],
        "summary": "Trigger a reporting read model refresh",
        "description": "Enqueues an asynchronous refresh of the reporting read model. The refresh runs decoupled from the payment write path and records the source watermark on completion. Returns the current refresh status.",
        "operationId": "refreshStats",
        "security": [{ "bearerAuth": [] }],
        "responses": {
          "202": {
            "description": "Refresh accepted and running asynchronously",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/StatsRefreshStatus" }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" },
          "403": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/Forbidden" },
          "409": {
            "description": "A refresh is already in progress",
            "content": {
              "application/json": { "schema": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/StatsRefreshStatus" } }
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "get": {
        "tags": ["Admin"],
        "summary": "Get reporting read model refresh status",
        "description": "Returns the current refresh status and source watermark of the reporting read model.",
        "operationId": "getStatsRefreshStatus",
        "security": [{ "bearerAuth": [] }],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Current refresh status",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/StatsRefreshStatus" }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" },
          "403": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/Forbidden" }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "components": {
    "securitySchemes": {
      "bearerAuth": {
        "type": "http",
        "scheme": "bearer",
        "bearerFormat": "JWT"
      }
    },
    "parameters": {
      "PageParam": {
        "name": "page",
        "in": "query",
        "description": "Page number (1-based)",
        "schema": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 1, "default": 1 }
      },
      "LimitParam": {
        "name": "limit",
        "in": "query",
        "description": "Maximum number of items per page",
        "schema": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 100, "default": 20 }
      },
      "CursorParam": {
        "name": "cursor",
        "in": "query",
        "description": "Opaque cursor for pagination",
        "schema": { "type": "string" }
      },
      "TagIdParam": {
        "name": "id",
        "in": "path",
        "required": true,
        "description": "Tag identifier",
        "schema": { "type": "string" }
      },
      "AddressParam": {
        "name": "address",
        "in": "path",
        "required": true,
        "description": "Stellar account address",
        "schema": { "type": "string" }
      },
      "TokenParam": {
        "name": "token",
        "in": "path",
        "required": true,
        "description": "Token identifier (asset code or contract address)",
        "schema": { "type": "string" }
      },
      "IdempotencyKeyParam": {
        "name": "X-Idempotency-Key",
        "in": "header",
        "required": false,
        "description": "Client-generated idempotency key scoped to the authenticated principal and operation. Reusing the key for retries of the same logical operation returns the original outcome and sets `X-Idempotent-Replay: true`. Generate a fresh key per logical operation; keys expire.",
        "schema": { "type": "string", "minLength": 8, "maxLength": 255 }
      }
    },
    "responses": {
      "ApiErrorResponse": {
        "description": "A standardized API error. Clients map `error.code` to a central catalog for actionable, accessible recovery guidance, fall back safely for unknown codes, honor `error.retryable` for retry behavior, and display `reference_id` for support correlation.",
        "headers": {
          "X-Idempotent-Replay": { "$ref": "#/components/headers/IdempotentReplayHeader" }
        },
        "content": {
          "application/json": {
            "schema": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error" }
          }
        }
      },
      "BadRequest": {
        "description": "Invalid request",
        "content": {
          "application/json": {
            "schema": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error" }
          }
        }
      },
      "Unauthorized": {
        "description": "Authentication required or invalid credentials",
        "content": {
          "application/json": {
            "schema": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error" }
          }
        }
      },
      "Forbidden": {
        "description": "Authenticated but not permitted (e.g. not the original owner)",
        "content": {
          "application/json": {
            "schema": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error" }
          }
        }
      },
      "NotFound": {
        "description": "Resource not found",
        "content": {
          "application/json": {
            "schema": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error" }
          }
        }
      },
      "Conflict": {
        "description": "State transition conflict (name reserved, stale restore proof, or concurrent transition lost)",
        "content": {
          "application/json": { "schema": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error" } }
        }
      },
      "Gone": {
        "description": "Reservation window expired; the tag can no longer be restored",
        "content": {
          "application/json": { "schema": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error" } }
        }
      }
    },
    "headers": {
      "IdempotentReplayHeader": {
        "description": "Present on responses to requests carrying `X-Idempotency-Key`. `true` indicates the response is a replay of a previously processed request; `false` indicates first-time processing.",
        "schema": { "type": "boolean" }
      }
    },
    "schemas": {
      "TagInput": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": ["username", "address"],
        "properties": {
          "username": { "type": "string" },
          "address": { "type": "string" }
        }
      },
      "Tag": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": ["id", "username", "address"],
        "properties": {
          "id": { "type": "string" },
          "username": { "type": "string" },
          "address": { "type": "string" },
          "createdAt": { "type": "string", "format": "date-time" },
          "deletedAt": { "type": "string", "format": "date-time" }
        }
      },
      "TagList": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": ["data"],
        "properties": {
          "data": { "type": "array", "items": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Tag" } },
          "totalCount": { "type": "integer" },
          "totalPages": { "type": "integer" },
          "currentPage": { "type": "integer" }
        }
      },
      "ActivityList": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": ["data"],
        "properties": {
          "data": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "object", "additionalProperties": true } },
          "nextCursor": { "type": "string" },
          "hasMore": { "type": "boolean" }
        }
      },
      "Stats": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "Aggregate metrics and the refresh watermark for the reporting read model.",
        "additionalProperties": true
      },
      "StatsRefreshStatus": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": ["status"],
        "properties": {
          "status": { "type": "string", "enum": ["idle", "refreshing", "succeeded", "failed"] },
          "sourceWatermark": { "type": "string", "format": "date-time" },
          "startedAt": { "type": "string", "format": "date-time" },
          "completedAt": { "type": "string", "format": "date-time" },
          "error": { "type": "string" }
        }
      },
      "Error": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": ["success", "error"],
        "properties": {
          "success": { "type": "boolean", "const": false },
          "error": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": ["code", "message", "retryable"],
            "properties": {
              "code": {
                "type": "string",
                "enum": [
                  "INVALID_INPUT",
                  "UNAUTHENTICATED",
                  "FORBIDDEN",
                  "NOT_FOUND",
                  "METHOD_NOT_ALLOWED",
                  "GONE",
                  "CONFLICT",
                  "PAYLOAD_TOO_LARGE",
                  "UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA_TYPE",
                  "VALIDATION_FAILED",
                  "RATE_LIMITED",
                  "INTERNAL_ERROR",
                  "UPSTREAM_ERROR",
                  "SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE"
                ]
              },
              "message": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Safe, human-readable message. Clients should prefer their central code-to-message catalog and use this only as a fallback."
              },
              "retryable": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "description": "Whether the client may retry the same operation. When `true`, retry with backoff (reusing the same `X-Idempotency-Key` for state-changing requests). When `false`, do not auto-retry; surface remediation guidance instead."
              },
              "details": {
                "type": "array",
                "items": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "required": ["field", "message"],
                  "properties": {
                    "field": { "type": "string" },
                    "message": { "type": "string" }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "correlation_id": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Opaque tracing identifier. Safe to display and log; never contains internal details."
          },
          "reference_id": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Safe, opaque, non-sensitive reference identifier for support correlation. Display to the user when present. Never a secret and never contains server internals."
          }
        }
      },
      "HealthStatus": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": ["status", "timestamp", "database", "redis", "horizon"],
        "properties": {
          "status": { "type": "string", "enum": ["UP"] },
          "timestamp": { "type": "string", "format": "date-time" },
          "database": { "type": "string", "enum": ["up"] },
          "redis": { "type": "string", "enum": ["up", "not configured"] },
          "horizon": { "type": "string", "enum": ["up"] }
        }
      },
      "FederationEntry": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": ["stellar_address", "account_id"],
        "properties": {
          "stellar_address": { "type": "string" },
          "account_id": { "type": "string" },
          "memo_type": { "type": "string" },
          "memo": { "type": "string" }
        }
      },
      "LookupResult": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "username": { "type": "string" },
          "address": { "type": "string" },
          "primary": { "type": "string" },
          "usernames": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" } },
          "data": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "object", "additionalProperties": true } },
          "totalCount": { "type": "integer" },
          "totalPages": { "type": "integer" },
          "currentPage": { "type": "integer" }
        }
      },
      "RestoreTagInput": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": ["deletedAt"],
        "properties": {
          "deletedAt": {
            "type": "string",
            "format": "date-time",
            "description": "The `deletedAt` value observed at deletion time; used as restoration proof. A mismatch is rejected with 409 Conflict."
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
